      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"We don\u0027t have any direct tests that exercise the real hardware OTP code.\"\nIf you exclude your changes to otp_key.c, the test_otp_key() function calls the real hardware OTP read function. This is directly exercising the real OTP code in the same way that the new function test_otp_key_read() is. It also has the benefit of provisioning unprovisioned hardware where applicable such that the test wouldn\u0027t fail. Further, it avoids adding new code where it is unnecessary. Based on these reasons, I think this CL is better with just the changes to otp_key.mocklist which only use the mock on host.",
